# Real libc puts body: prologue pushes cost 12 cycles.
# The 12.00 below is the push latency column. Only the callee-saved pushes
# are pinned as an unordered set; their order and the mov immediates move
# with the libc release.
# REQUIRES: x86_64, system-libc
# RUN: perf analyze /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6:puts -e index,assembly,latency 2>&1 | %FileCheck %s
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
# CHECK: index assembly latency
# CHECK-NEXT: endbr64
# CHECK-DAG: push r14 12.00
# CHECK-DAG: push r13 12.00
# CHECK-DAG: push r12 12.00
# CHECK-DAG: push rbx 12.00
# CHECK-NOT: Traceback
